            "review_text": "Listenup696\nTuan Chau Island, Vietnam2 contributions\n1\nAvoid!!!!\nJun 2018 • Couples\nIt was 1:30pm on a Friday. We just landed in Hanoi and starving. From our hotel we walked past Mango beer cafe and though this would be a good place to eat. We were wrong. When we walked through the door no one greeted us apart from this lady not in uniform like everyone else (possibly owner). She seated us down and handed us a massive menu. Once I flipped to the first page she asked me what I wanted (no time to look at all). I said that I wanted a coke and she replied with a rude “NO” so I ordered a sprite and again she shouted “NO” so I got a watermelon juice instead. We then ordered out food, I wanted to try seafood salad which again she said “NO” and I pointed at something else - again she said “NO”. (Like is she going to pick what I eat or what?) finally I pointed to a noodle and beef stir fry and she started writing it down.. 🙄 my partner ordered a pizza (if you would call it that- frozen pizza is so much better that what he was served) . My “stir fry” came out, I couldn’t recognise it because it looked like 2 mins noodles toss with some meat and vegetables with no flavour? We left in a hurry as we were feeling very unwelcome. Looking across the room another waiter was cleaning up the table and he just toss the left over beer from a glass on the floor.. if that’s how they clean I don’t even want to know how they cook food. Overall disgusting service and food was below average. Will we return? Don’t hold your breath. We later went to another restaurant 5 mins after leaving this place to order a proper meal and we were treated like how we should be for paying customer.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 2, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
